  #line-at(322.273pt, 492pt, " layer, confirming uniform elemental distribution ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 510.96pt, "and indicating that the visible stratification arises from morphological, not compositional, variations. (c) ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 529.92pt, "Thermal model schematic used in SPS signal fitting, incorporating 19 intrinsic parameters and their grouping ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 548.88pt, "into 13 key combined parameters that govern heat diffusion. The diagram also defines the labeling system for ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 567.84pt, "these combined parameters, which are central to sensitivity and SVD analysis.  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 609.84pt, "3.2. Measurement procedure ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 635.04pt, "We employed a variable spot size and multi-frequency approach based on the SPS technique to probe multiple ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 660.48pt, "thermal parameters of the multilayered system. Specifically, high modulation frequencies (in the MHz range) were ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 685.68pt, "used to probe the thermal properties of the topmost layers, while low modulation frequencies (in the kHz range) ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 710.88pt, "probed the substrate. A large laser spot size reduced sensitivity to in-plane thermal transport, whereas a small spot ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 736.32pt, "size enhanced it. To illustrate the measurement process, we present an example of room-temperature ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 761.52pt, "measurements on this multilayered SOI system.  ")
]

