  #line-at(56.88pt, 170.16pt, "confirmed that variations in these values had negligible effect on the fitted results.  ")
  #line-at(78.88pt, 195.36pt, "To extract the seven fitted parameters, we employed a hybrid optimization algorithm combining particle ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 220.8pt, "swarm optimization (PSO) with the quasi-Newton method to fit the four signal sets in Figures 3 and 4. This ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 246pt, "hybrid approach achieved not only improved accuracy but also significantly higher computational efficiency ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 271.44pt, "than the commonly used MATLAB function “lsqnonlin”. Briefly, PSO—a global optimization scheme ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 296.64pt, "inspired by swarm intelligence—explores the parameter space to identify global optima. While highly robust ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 321.84pt, "and effective at avoiding local minima in high-dimensional spaces, PSO’s convergence rate declines after ~10 ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 347.28pt, "iterations. To address this limitation, we transitioned to the quasi-Newton method, a gradient-based local ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 372.48pt, "optimizer, which rapidly refines the solution to high precision. By integrating the global exploration strength ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 397.92pt, "of PSO with the fast local convergence of quasi-Newton, we achieve efficient and accurate parameter ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 423.12pt, "estimation.  ")
