  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(204.645pt, 558.24pt, ") at 100 K, our method remains effective for thinner films, such as the 1.6 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 583.92pt, "μ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(62.401pt, 583.92pt, "m-thick sample, due to the enhanced sensitivity provided by the variable-spot-size, multi-frequency SPS ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 609.12pt, "approach across a broad range of modulation frequencies and laser spot sizes. This comparison underscores ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 634.56pt, "several advantages of the SPS method over TDTR, including its ability to extract a larger set of thermal ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 659.76pt, "parameters simultaneously, reduced uncertainty in measured values, and superior applicability to thinner films ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 684.96pt, "and low-temperature conditions where TDTR becomes less effective. Overall, the excellent agreement ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 710.4pt, "between our measurements, prior experimental data, and first-principles predictions confirms the accuracy and ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 735.6pt, "robustness of the current method.  ")
